#: ../../source/refs/release_notes.rst:1185
msgid ""
"We have now removed the ``disable_contact_processing`` flag from the "
":class:`isaaclab.sim.SimulationCfg` to not have the user worry about "
"these intricacies of the simulator. The flag is always True by default "
"unless a contact sensor is created (which will internally set this flag "
"to False)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/refs/release_notes.rst:1189
msgid ""
"Previously, the flag ``disable_contact_processing`` led to confusion "
"about its behavior. As the name suggests, the flag controls the contact "
"reporting from the underlying physics engine, PhysX. Disabling this flag "
"(note the double negation) means that PhysX collects the contact "
"information from its solver and allows reporting them to the user. "
"Enabling this flag means this operation is not performed and the overhead"
" of it is avoided."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/refs/release_notes.rst:1196
msgid ""
"Many of our examples (for instance, the locomotion environments) were "
"setting this flag to True which meant the contacts should **not** get "
"reported. However, this issue was not noticed earlier since GPU "
"simulation bypasses this flag, and only CPU simulation gets affected. "
"Running the same examples on CPU device led to different behaviors "
"because of this reason."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/refs/release_notes.rst:1202
msgid ""
"Existing users, who currently set this flag themselves, should receive a "
"deprecated warning mentioning the removal of this flag and the switch to "
"the new default behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/refs/release_notes.rst:1206
msgid "Switch to older rendering settings to improve render quality"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/refs/release_notes.rst:1208
msgid ""
"With the IsaacLab 2.0.0 release, we switched to new render settings aimed"
" at improving tiled-rendering performance, but at the cost of reduced "
"rendering quality. This change particularly affected dome lighting in the"
" scene, which is the default in many of our examples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/refs/release_notes.rst:1212
msgid ""
"As reported by several users, this change negatively impacted render "
"quality, even in cases where it wasn't necessary (such as when recording "
"videos of the simulation). In response to this feedback, we have reverted"
" to the previous render settings by default to restore the quality users "
"expected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/refs/release_notes.rst:1217
msgid ""
"For users looking to trade render quality for speed, we will provide "
"guidelines in the future."
msgstr ""

