#: ../../source/refs/release_notes.rst:1748
msgid "Setting the simulation device from CLI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/refs/release_notes.rst:1750
msgid ""
"Previously, users could specify the device through the command line "
"argument ``--device_id``. However, this made it ambiguous when users "
"wanted to set the device to CPU. Thus, instead of the device ID, users "
"need to specify the device explicitly through the argument ``--device``. "
"The valid options for the device name are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/refs/release_notes.rst:1755
msgid "\"cpu\": runs simulation on CPU"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/refs/release_notes.rst:1756
msgid "\"cuda\": runs simulation on GPU with device ID at default index"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/refs/release_notes.rst:1757
msgid ""
"\"cuda:N\": runs simulation on GPU with device ID at ``N``. For instance,"
" \"cuda:0\" will use device at index \"0\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/refs/release_notes.rst:1759
msgid ""
"Due to the above change, the command line interaction with some of the "
"scripts has changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/refs/release_notes.rst:1774
msgid "Renaming of teleoperation device CLI in standalone scripts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/refs/release_notes.rst:1776
msgid ""
"Since ``--device`` is now an argument provided by the AppLauncher, it "
"conflicted with the command-line argument used for specifying the "
"teleoperation-device in some of the standalone scripts. Thus, to fix this"
" conflict, the teleoperation-device now needs to be specified through "
"``--teleop_device`` argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/refs/release_notes.rst:1794
msgid "Using Python-version of container utility script"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/refs/release_notes.rst:1796
msgid ""
"The prior `container.sh <https://github.com/isaac-"
"sim/IsaacLab/blob/v1.1.0/docker/container.sh>`_ became quite complex as "
"it had many different use cases in one script. For instance, building a "
"docker image for \"base\" or \"ros2\", as well as cluster deployment. As "
"more users wanted to have the flexibility to overlay their own docker "
"settings, maintaining this bash script became cumbersome. Hence, we "
"migrated its features into a Python script in this release. Additionally,"
" we split the cluster-related utilities into their own script inside the "
"``docker/cluster`` directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/refs/release_notes.rst:1802
msgid ""
"We still maintain backward compatibility for ``container.sh``. "
"Internally, it calls the Python script ``container.py``. We request users"
" to use the Python script directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/refs/release_notes.rst:1820
msgid "Using separate directories for logging videos in RL workflows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/refs/release_notes.rst:1822
msgid ""
"Previously, users could record videos during the RL training by "
"specifying the ``--video`` flag to the ``train.py`` script. The videos "
"would be saved inside the ``videos`` directory in the corresponding log "
"directory of the run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/refs/release_notes.rst:1826
msgid ""
"Since many users requested to also be able to record videos while "
"inferencing the policy, recording videos have also been added to the "
"``play.py`` script. Since changing the prefix of the video file names is "
"not possible, the videos from the train and play scripts are saved inside"
" the ``videos/train`` and ``videos/play`` directories, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/refs/release_notes.rst:1832
msgid "Drops support for the tiled camera with Isaac Sim 4.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/refs/release_notes.rst:1834
msgid ""
"Various fixes have been made to the tiled camera rendering pipeline in "
"Isaac Sim 4.2. This made supporting the tiled camera with Isaac Sim 4.1 "
"difficult. Hence, for the best experience, we advice switching to Isaac "
"Sim 4.2 with this release of Isaac Lab."
msgstr ""

